From da9b72de5d39927f24089d48592593b59132b192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:18:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): apply stored script options for named posts
 and warn on mismatch

Resolve a named or file-based post in `cam.post` / MCP `post` to its `PostRef`
so `program_options_for_script` reads stored `PostScriptOptions` across both
single-mount and multi-mount posting, and match `.cps` files canonically. When
an explicit post differs from the document or setup's configured post and leaves
stored `script_options` unapplied, report a clear `warning` naming the setup,
post, and unapplied option keys.

Fixes #2190
